    "pdp_faqs_MicmxB": {
      "type": "pdp-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_yNgRPL": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are {{ product.metafields.custom.course_code.value }} credits recognized by Ontario universities?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. All Ontario universities accept OEO credits as official OSSD credits. OEO is a Ministry-inspected private school (BSID #882902) and your credit appears on an official Ontario transcript. Admissions offices at the University of Toronto, McMaster, Western, Queen's, York, Ottawa, and all other Ontario universities treat these credits identically to those earned at any public or private day school.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_hk7fNA": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What's the difference between the Canada and International price?",
            "answer": "<p>Students currently residing in Canada pay $599 CAD. Students outside Canada pay a different rate to account for currency differences and administrative costs related to international transcript handling. Both groups receive the same course content, the same Ontario-certified teacher, and the same official OSSD credit. Contact us if you have questions about the international pricing before enrolling.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_gnnpm4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need to be online at specific times?",
            "answer": "<p>No. {{ product.metafields.custom.course_code.value }} at OEO is fully asynchronous and self-paced. You access course materials, complete assignments, and submit your work whenever works for you, day or night, weekday or weekend. There are no scheduled live classes, no mandatory login times, and no fixed pacing requirements. You control your schedule entirely.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_9GhqY7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does teacher feedback work?",
            "answer": "<p>{{ product.metafields.custom.teacher.value.teacher_name.value }}, your Ontario-certified Teacher, personally reviews each assignment you submit and returns detailed written feedback within 24 hours on weekdays. You'll receive comments on what you did well, where marks were deducted, and specific guidance on what to focus on next. This one-on-one feedback loop is one of the biggest advantages of learning at OEO compared to a traditional classroom where a teacher is managing 30 students at once.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Ai9UKw": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the refund policy?",
            "answer": "<p>If you haven't yet accessed any course content, you can request a full refund within 7 days of purchase. Once course units have been opened and accessed, refunds are reviewed on a case-by-case basis. We always try to find a fair solution. If something comes up, reach out to us at <a href=\"mailto:info@ontarioeducationonline.ca\" target=\"_blank\">info@ontarioeducationonline.ca </a>and we'll work with you.<br/><br/><br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_yX96G8": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How quickly can I complete the course?",
            "answer": "<p>Most students complete {{ product.metafields.custom.course_code.value }} in 4 to 8 weeks. Students who study 3 to 4 hours per day typically finish in 4 to 5 weeks. If you have a university application deadline approaching, book a guidance session and we'll help you plan a realistic study schedule that fits your timeline. There's no minimum time requirement. You work at whatever pace suits you.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
